{"records":[{"id":"y8dndzn3mg","title":"Genome-scale CRISPR screen identifies TMEM41B as a critical host factor required for coronavirus replication","description":"These data are part of the Supplemental Items associated with the manuscript entitled \"Genome-scale CRISPR screen identifies TMEM41B as a critical host factor required for coronavirus replication\". These files include Supplementary Data file 1-4.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2021-03-16T10:34:13.579Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/y8dndzn3mg","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/y8dndzn3mg"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Limeng","last_name":"Sun","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Virus","Screening","CRISPR/Cas9"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"4mb5kjywkj","title":"Western Blot raw data of the manuscript titled \"In vivo CRISPR knockout screen identifies p47 as a suppressor for HER2+ breast cancer metastasis by regulating NEMO trafficking and autophagy flux\"","description":"The raw images of WB is for the reviewers' request when reviewing the manuscript titled \"In vivo CRISPR knockout screen identifies p47 as a suppressor for HER2+ breast cancer metastasis by regulating NEMO trafficking and autophagy flux\".","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-12-04T00:26:32.621Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/4mb5kjywkj","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/4mb5kjywkj"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Mingang","last_name":"Hao","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Western Blot"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"wxk9gnw22r","title":"Quantitative temporal proteomic analysis of vaccinia virus infection reveals regulation of histone deacetylases by an interferon antagonist","description":"Vaccinia virus (VACV) has numerous immune evasion strategies, including multiple mechanisms of inhibition of IRF-3, NF-κB and type I interferon (IFN) signaling. Here, we use highly multiplexed proteomics to quantify ~9,000 cellular proteins and ~80% of viral proteins at seven time points throughout VACV infection. 265 cellular proteins are downregulated >2 fold by VACV, including putative natural killer cell ligands and IFN-stimulated genes. Two thirds of these viral targets, including the class II histone deacetylase HDAC5, are degraded proteolytically during infection. In follow-up analysis, we demonstrate that HDAC5 restricts replication of both VACV and herpes simplex virus type 1. By generating a protein-based temporal classification of VACV gene expression, we identify protein C6, a multifunctional IFN antagonist, as being necessary and sufficient for proteasomal degradation of HDAC5. Our approach thus identifies both a host antiviral factor and a viral mechanism of innate immune evasion.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2019-05-07T17:03:10.299Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/wxk9gnw22r","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/wxk9gnw22r"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Michael","last_name":"Weekes","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Proteomics"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"8xhv88c7wt","title":"Genome-wide screening in human kidney organoids identifies developmental and disease-related aspects of nephrogenesis","description":"Human organoids allow the study of proliferation, lineage specification, and three-dimensional tissue development. Here, we present a genome-wide CRISPR screen in iPSC-derived kidney organoids. The combination of inducible genome editing, longitudinal sampling and endpoint sorting of tubular and stromal cells generated a complex, high-quality dataset uncovering a broad spectrum of insightful biology from early development to ‘adult’ epithelial morphogenesis. Our functional dataset allows improving mesoderm induction by ROCK inhibition, contains monogenetic and complex trait kidney disease genes, confirms two additional CAKUT genes (CCDC170 and MYH7B), and provides a large candidate list of ciliopathy-related genes. Finally, the identification of a cis-inhibitory effect of Jagged1 controlling epithelial proliferation shows how mosaic knockouts in pooled CRISPR screening can discover ways of communication between heterogeneous cell populations in complex tissues. Collectively, these data serve both as a rich resource for the kidney community and as a benchmark for future iPSC-derived organoid CRISPR screens.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2021-11-29T13:48:59.335Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/8xhv88c7wt","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/8xhv88c7wt"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Rosemarie","last_name":"Ungricht","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Philipp","last_name":"Hoppe","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Screening","CRISPR"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"ztg7pxr6ch","title":"STT3A is essential for Wnt signaling and represents a target for cancers driven by RNF43 deficiency","description":"This dataset contains the original raw and analyzed data supporting the manuscript “STT3A is essential for Wnt signaling and represents a target for cancers driven by RNF43 deficiency”. The study identifies STT3A as an essential regulator of the Wnt signaling pathway and a potential therapeutic target for RNF43-deficient cancers. Included data were generated from key experiments, including Wnt reporter assays (DDT), Western blotting (WB), and CRISPR screen, and other experiments central to the study","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-10-13T11:26:58.874Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/ztg7pxr6ch","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/ztg7pxr6ch"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Zhengjin","last_name":"He","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Cell Biology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"znm8dm7rb8","title":"The Transcription Factor ThPOK Orchestrates Stochastic Interchromosomal Interactions Required for IFN-β Virus Inducible Gene Expression.Nikopoulou et al.","description":"Raw data published in the manuscript The Transcription Factor ThPOK Orchestrates Stochastic Interchromosomal Interactions Required for IFN-β Virus Inducible Gene Expression by Nikopoulou et al.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2018-06-20T10:06:41.931Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/znm8dm7rb8","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/znm8dm7rb8"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Chrysa","last_name":"Nikopoulou","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Dimitris","last_name":"Thanos","orcid":null},{"first_name":"George","last_name":"Panagopoulos","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["DNA Interactions with Proteins","Immunoprecipitation","Fluorescence Microscopy","Electrophoretic Mobility-Shift Assay","Western Blot","DNA Footprinting"],"journal_issn":["10972765"]},{"id":"n4m3mghz5w","title":"The Transcription Factor ThPOK Orchestrates Stochastic Interchromosomal Interactions Required for IFN-β Virus Inducible Gene Expression. Nikopoulou C., Panagopoulos G. et al.","description":"Raw data of the manuscript The Transcription Factor ThPOK Orchestrates Stochastic Interchromosomal Interactions Required for IFN-β Virus Inducible Gene Expression. Nikopoulou C., Panagopoulos G. et al.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2018-06-20T10:30:07.562Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/n4m3mghz5w","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/n4m3mghz5w"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Chrysa","last_name":"Nikopoulou","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Dimitris","last_name":"Thanos","orcid":nul